\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For every complex von Neumann algebra M and every integer $k\geq 2$, is each bounded k-cocycle with coefficients in M a bounded coboundary, that is $H^k(M,M)=0$, without a complete-boundedness or separability restriction?

\subsection{Short English statement}
For every complex von Neumann algebra M and every integer $k\geq 2$, is each bounded k-cocycle with coefficients in M a bounded coboundary, that is $H^k(M,M)=0$, without a complete-boundedness or separability restriction?

